<problem>
<!-- <title>Derivative of quotient of quadratic functions</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="c1" numToSelect="3" withReplacement="true" from="-10" to=" 10" exclude="0" />

<selectFromSequence name="temp1" numToSelect="3" withReplacement="true" from="-10" to=" 10" exclude="0" />
<select name="a1" numToSelect="4" withReplacement="false">
<option>$temp1[1]</option>
<option>$temp1[2]</option>
<option>$temp1[3]</option>
<option><math>0</math></option>
</select>


<select name="function"> f g m p r u v w</select>
<select name="x"> x y z s t</select>

<math name="numerator" simplify="full">$a1[1][1] *$x ^2+$a1[2][1] *$x +$c1[1] </math>
<math name="denominator" simplify="full">$a1[3][1] *$x ^2+$a1[4][1] *$x +$c1[2] </math>
<math name="quotient" simplify="full">$numerator /$denominator </math>
<derivative name="derivative" simplify="full" variables="$x">$quotient</derivative>
<math name="derivative2" simplify="full" expand="true">$derivative </math>
<derivative name="d_numerator" simplify="full" variables="$x">$numerator</derivative>
<derivative name="d_denominator" simplify="full" variables="$x">$denominator</derivative>
<math name="numerator_of_derivative" simplify="full" expand="true">$denominator *$d_numerator -$numerator *$d_denominator </math>
<math name="deriv" simplify="full">d$function/d$x</math>
<selectFromSequence name="phrasing" from="1" to="4" />
<!-- <math name='derivative_sign_error_detection' simplify='full' >$numerator_of_derivative /$denominator ^2 </math> -->

</setup>


<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$phrasing = 1">
Let <m>$function ($x ) = $quotient </m>.  Find <m>$deriv </m>.

</case><case condition="$phrasing = 2">
Calculate <m>$deriv </m>, where  <m>$function ($x ) = $quotient </m>. 

</case><case condition="$phrasing = 3">
Calculate the derivative of <m>$function ($x ) = $quotient </m>.

</case><else>
Differentiate the function <m>$function ($x ) = $quotient </m>.

</else>
</conditionalContent>


<p><m>$deriv  =</m> 
<answer forceFullCheckWorkButton="true">
<award>$derivative </award>
<!-- <award credit='0.9' nSignErrorsMatched="1" feedbackCodes='onesignerror'>$derivative </award> -->
<!-- <award credit='0.81' nSignErrorsMatched="2" feedbackCodes='twosignerrors'>$derivative </award> -->
<!-- <award symbolicEquality='true'>$derivative_sign_error_detection </award> -->
<!-- <award credit='0.9' symbolicEquality='true' nSignErrorsMatched="1" feedbackCodes='onesignerror'>$derivative_sign_error_detection </award> -->
<!-- <award credit='0.81' symbolicEquality='true' nSignErrorsMatched="2" feedbackCodes='twosignerrors'>$derivative_sign_error_detection </award> -->
</answer>
<!-- <copy prop="feedbacks" source="answer1" /> -->
</p>

<hint>


<paragraphs>
<title>Helpful pages</title>
<ul>
<li><ref to="doenet:7KNaZhtcLkYEubRxQt2Ak4">The derivative of a power function</ref></li>
<li><ref to="doenet:7KXg34rBKDhBUUnmi58mwv">Derivatives of polynomials</ref></li>
<li><ref to="doenet:7LMCto3Hr81zxLMzwiiARp">The quotient rule for differentiation</ref>
</li>
</ul>
</paragraphs>
</hint>


<solution>
Using the 
<ref to="doenet:7LMCto3Hr81zxLMzwiiARp">The quotient rule for differentiation</ref>
, 
<md>
  <mrow>\frac{ d$function }{ d$x }\amp =  \frac{ ($denominator  ) \frac{ d }{ d$x } ($numerator )  - ($numerator ) \frac{ d }{ d$x } ($denominator  ) }{ ($denominator )^2 }</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp =  \frac{ ($denominator  ) ($d_numerator ) - ($numerator )($d_denominator ) }{ ($denominator )^2 }</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp =  \frac{ $numerator_of_derivative  }{ ($denominator )^2 }.</mrow>
</md>
We could multiply out the denominator <m>($denominator )^2</m>, but there is no real advantage for doing so.


</solution>


</problem>